# Project docs — source of truth

Before implementing features, refactors, or schema/UI changes, **read the relevant docs** in `docs/`. Do not drift from the intended plan without updating the doc first.

## When to read what

| Task | Read first |
|------|------------|
| Solution structure, layers, folders, services, controllers | `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` |
| Entities, tables, relationships, enums, business rules | `docs/DATABASE_SCHEMA.md` |
| Colors, typography, components, UI tokens | `docs/DESIGN-SYSTEM.md` |
| Dashboard CSS split + Tailwind-first | `.cursor/rules/dashboard-css.mdc` |
| Branches, PRs, merge flow | `docs/GIT-WORKFLOW.md` |
| Unit tests (MSTest, DataAccess, Business) | `docs/UNIT-TESTING.md` |

## Required behavior

1. **Start non-trivial work** by skimming the matching doc(s) — especially for new modules, EF entities, or dashboard sections.
2. **Follow documented conventions** (Clean Architecture layers; entity folders **Operationnel / Vente / Achat** + `Common/` for shared refs; DTO vs ViewModel; URL sections matching sidebar; ZAHO tokens; no Bon de Préparation).
3. **If the plan must change**, update the relevant `docs/*.md` in the same change (or propose the doc update before coding).
4. **Do not** introduce patterns contradicting `ARCHITECTURE.md` (e.g. DbContext in controllers, entities in views, new accent colors without `DESIGN-SYSTEM.md`).

## Quick alignment checks

- New table/entity → exists or is added in `DATABASE_SCHEMA.md`?
- New page/module → fits layer + folder layout in `ARCHITECTURE.md`?
- New UI → uses tokens from `DESIGN-SYSTEM.md` / `Styles/app.css` `@theme`?
- Git workflow → feature branch → PR to `dev` per `GIT-WORKFLOW.md`?
- New service/repo tests → follow `UNIT-TESTING.md` (method groups, Covered checklist)?

When in doubt, read the doc rather than guessing.
